            <div xml:id="d839">

                <pb facs="0793" n="693" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg693"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">311.6124/6: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Commissioner at
                        Riga</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gade</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-12-24T13:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 24,
                                1919—1 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your 48 December 21, 1 a.m. United States transport <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Buford</hi> sailed from New York December 21st having on board 249 Russian
                    subjects and will reach Libau not later than January 12. You will be advised of
                    ship’s progress.</p>
                <p>F. W. Berkshire, Immigration Inspector in charge of party, carries letter of
                    introduction to you.</p>
                <p>Please perfect arrangements as far as possible before arrival of ship. You or a
                    responsible representative of yours should be at the port. Berkshire’s
                    instructions are simply to place himself in your hands and be guided by the
                    arrangements which you have made.</p>
                <p>Food of a value equivalent to cost of transporting Russians estimated at $4000
                    will be placed at disposal of Latvian authorities either being shipped by first
                    opportunity or found for them in Europe.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
